//? Title: Hungarian Assignment: Prices, Paths and an Optimality Check
//? Subtitle: Actual primal-dual histories for finite square costs
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A worker's cheapest task may already belong to another worker. The Hungarian
method resolves this conflict by repricing an alternating search and then
flipping an augmenting path. We start with a two-worker example that must
reassign its first choice, preserve the original three-worker example, and check
the final permutation against row/column dual prices. Negative costs, ties,
arithmetic limits and complete history admission are explicit. Every history
comes from the solve that produced the answer; no path is replayed.
)
\toc

> Start with a conflict

For costs \(C=((1,2),(1,100))\), both workers prefer task zero. The first row
initially takes it, but keeping that choice would cost 101. The optimum sends
worker zero to task one and worker one to task zero, costing three. Task boxes
in the diagram are reordered to align the final matched pairs; printed labels
retain their original indices. The event table shows the actual reprices and
completed augmentations, including the second search's zero delta and final
positive delta. A zero delta can expose an already-tight edge; it is not a stop.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hungarian_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto t = dm::algorithms::hungarian_trace({{1, 2}, {1, 100}});
    std::print("| boundary | introduced row | expanded row | next task | delta | task 0 owner | task 1 " "owner |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.events) {
        auto owner = [&](std::size_t j) {
            return e.column_to_row[j] == dm::algorithms::kAssignmentUnmatched
                ? std::string("free") : std::to_string(e.column_to_row[j]);
        };
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
                   e.kind == dm::algorithms::AssignmentEventKind::Reprice
                   ? "reprice" : "augment", e.introduced_row, e.expanded_row,
                   e.next_column, e.delta, owner(0), owner(1));
    }
    const auto d = dm::algorithms::assignment_diagnostics(t.costs, t.run);
    std::print("Primal {}, dual {}, gap {}, minimum slack {}, matched residual {}.\n",
               d.primal, d.dual, d.gap, d.minimum_slack,
               d.maximum_matched_residual);
    dm::algorithms::assignment_diagram(t.costs, t.run).save_svg(
        "build/hungarian_tiny.svg");
}
```
