> Work, storage and what the measurements mean

At most n columns are expanded per augmentation, each scan considers at most n
columns, and there are n augmentations: O(n³) ordinary time and O(n) auxiliary
storage, excluding the borrowed n² input and owned outputs. The trace copies n²
original costs and stores O(events·n) values; its observation work and storage
are additional. No timing claim follows from counting selected operations.

Two deterministic families show why a single growth curve is inadequate. With
zero diagonal and unit off-diagonal costs each new row immediately reaches its
own free task: n reprices and n² slack evaluations. With every cost zero,
ascending-column ties expand i columns while adding row i (one-based). The
number of reprices is n(n+1)/2, and slack evaluations are

$$
\sum_{i=1}^n\sum_{k=0}^{i-1}(n-k)=\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6}.
$$
\alttext(All-tied costs produce a sum-of-squares count of slack evaluations under the specified ascending-column tie policy.)

These are actual producing counts, checked against the formulas for these
specific families. They exclude validation, comparisons, allocation, copying,
final summation and trace observation; they are not CPU instruction totals.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hungarian_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    std::vector<double> sizes, diagonal, tied;
    std::print("| n | diagonal slack evaluations | tied slack evaluations | diagonal reprices | tied " "reprices |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64}) {
        const auto a =
            dm::algorithms::hungarian_run(dm::algorithms::assignment_work_costs(
                                          n));
        const auto b =
            dm::algorithms::hungarian_run(dm::algorithms::assignment_work_costs(
                                          n, true));
        if (a.work.slack_evaluations != n * n ||
            b.work.slack_evaluations != n * (n + 1) * (2 * n + 1) / 6 ||
            a.work.reprices != n || b.work.reprices != n * (n + 1) / 2)
            throw std::runtime_error("work formula");
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, a.work.slack_evaluations,
                   b.work.slack_evaluations, a.work.reprices, b.work.reprices);
        sizes.push_back(n);
        diagonal.push_back(a.work.slack_evaluations);
        tied.push_back(b.work.slack_evaluations);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(sizes, diagonal, "diagonal", {37, 99, 235}, 2).line(sizes, tied,
                                                               "all tied",
                                                               {220, 38, 38}, 2).title("Actual slack evaluations for two controlled families").x_label("rows and tasks n").y_label("slack evaluations").y_limits(0, 110000).save_svg("build/hungarian_work.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| n | diagonal slack evaluations | tied slack evaluations | diagonal reprices | tied reprices |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 2 | 4 | 5 | 2 | 3 |
| 4 | 16 | 30 | 4 | 10 |
| 8 | 64 | 204 | 8 | 36 |
| 16 | 256 | 1496 | 16 | 136 |
| 32 | 1024 | 11440 | 32 | 528 |
| 64 | 4096 | 89440 | 64 | 2080 |
\image(figures/hungarian_work.svg)
